<!--
  Fixture for backend/scripts/tests/gate-summary.tests.ps1: same real xunit v3 dynamic-skip shape
  as fixtures/skipped/ (total=31, passed=0, failed=0, notExecuted=0), but with a Unix-style
  <UnitTest storage="..."> path (forward slashes, no drive letter) — what a real .trx written by
  `dotnet test` on Linux CI (ubuntu-latest) looks like, as opposed to fixtures/skipped/'s
  Windows-authored backslash path.

  This exists because Get-SuiteName used to delegate to [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension,
  whose separator set is OS-conditional: Windows recognizes both '/' and '\', Unix recognizes ONLY
  '/'. A Windows-style storage path is silently mis-parsed when the *runtime* is Unix, and (by the
  same logic, reversed) nothing on this fixture depended on which OS the currently-running test
  host is; both fixtures must parse identically on both hosts. Not a real dotnet test output;
  hand-authored.
-->
